      "weight": 0.4,
      "score": 35,
      "reasoning": "This is an Objective (Mode A) criterion. The report provides detailed quantitative estimates and cites the benchmark values, but its primary results understate cumulative loss, the late-period rate, acceleration (18% versus 36%), and the 2023 record, while omitting the required quantitative comparison with Greenland and Antarctic ice-sheet losses; its uncertainty treatment is also acknowledged as likely underestimated."
     },
     {
      "index": 1,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.1,
      "score": 35,
      "reasoning": "This is Mode A. The figures quantitatively reproduce regional specific and total mass-change rates and broadly support the expected absolute ranking; combining Arctic Canada North and South yields a Canadian Arctic contribution comparable to the target. However, they do not report the required contribution percentages or the relative loss versus 2000 ice volume, so the −39%, −35%, −29%, −23%, and −20% comparisons cannot be verified directly."
     },
     {
      "index": 2,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.2,
      "score": 28,
      "reasoning": "This is Mode A because the criterion specifies quantitative inter-method biases and uncertainties. The report provides regional method comparisons and shows broadly positive altimetry offsets and small gravimetry offsets, including a large Southern Andes discrepancy, but it compares against a combined DEM-differencing-plus-glaciological product rather than DEM differencing alone, does not report the required aggregate 0.08 ± 0.08 and 0.02 ± 0.08 values, and omits the glaciological-site bias and range entirely; moreover, shared temporal downscaling makes the apparent interannual consistency partly imposed by construction."
     },
     {
      "index": 3,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.3,
      "score": 0,
      "reasoning": "Mode A: the target requires quantitative observation–projection comparisons and future scenario trajectories. None of the AI-generated figures shows model projections to 2040/2100, emission-scenario dependence, percentile ranges, or the 2023 exceedance of the AR6 low-end projection; they instead present observational reconstruction and validation plots only."
     }
